{
  "rationale": "The plant is split into perception (sensing obstacles) and motion (executing actions). The specification binds sensor outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, ensuring the robot explores when clear, recovers conservatively from obstacles, and only uses full_rotate as a last resort. All uncontrollable events are handled in every state, and recovery states are one-shot. The design prioritizes forward/random_walk in clear states, rotates away from side obstacles, and backs up on front obstacles.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception and motion to reflect the robot's architecture.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, progress-maximizing action selection and conservative recovery, ensuring transitions out of recovery states as soon as the path is clear."
  ],
